      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "To sync parameters by name they either have to transmit the name in every packet, or do stuff under the hood to reconcile the parameters for various platforms. \nPersonally I just blindly sync the parameters between PC/Quest, the only downside that an unused parameter brings is that maybe you forget they're unused?\nJust spitballing with names like VRCEmote Outfit Sword, I think 32 bytes would fit three parameters, compared to allocating the 32 bytes (256 bits) into 32 different integers.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
